  "decision_conditions": [
    "Prior to commencement of the development, details of fire protection and noise attenuation measures between floors must be submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority. These measures must be designed to minimise physical and visual impact on historic cornices and windows.\r\rReason: To ensure that the application of fire safety does not adversely affect the elements that contribute to the building's significance to safeguard the special architectural and historic interests of the building in accordance with Policy 30 of the Sutton Local Plan 2018 and to ensure that the development incorporates the necessary fire safety measures in accordance with the Mayor's London Plan Policy D12."
